<!--
  Slide 09 — Flow Metrics Snapshot (metrics 1-7)
  Type: content-slide
  Required tokens (substituted by render_deck.py from metrics.json):
    {{M1_MULT}}, {{M1_CONF}}, {{M1_CONF_LABEL}}     Flow Load
    {{M2_MULT}}, {{M2_CONF}}, {{M2_CONF_LABEL}}     Flow Velocity
    {{M3_MULT}}, {{M3_CONF}}, {{M3_CONF_LABEL}}     Flow Predictability
    {{M4_MULT}}, {{M4_CONF}}, {{M4_CONF_LABEL}}     Flow Active
    {{M5_MULT}}, {{M5_CONF}}, {{M5_CONF_LABEL}}     Flow Efficiency
    {{M6_MULT}}, {{M6_CONF}}, {{M6_CONF_LABEL}}     Flow Distribution (point-difference string,
                                                    no trailing × — see Rendering notes)
    {{M7_MULT}}, {{M7_CONF}}, {{M7_CONF_LABEL}}     Flow Time
  Required non-text visual: <table class="metric-table"> (satisfies Rule 5
  content-slide visual requirement; theme.css §Phase 9 styles this table).

  Authority: AAP §0.4.1 (file inventory enumerates this filename),
  §0.2.2 (Metrics 1-7 align with the Flow Framework — Flow Load,
  Velocity, Predictability, Active, Efficiency, Distribution, Time),
  §0.7.1 Rule 5 (content-slide constraints — max 4 bullets, ≤40 body
  words, ≥1 non-text visual, zero emoji, no fenced code blocks),
  §0.7.2.1 (canonical phrasing "Insufficient signal — [reason]" when
  data is lacking; MUST NOT fabricate or extrapolate), §0.7.2.2 Rule 3
  (Confidence Transparency — every derived metric carries a tag),
  §0.7.2.2 Rule 4 (Internal Consistency — values here must match
  acceleration-report.md, Traceability Matrix, and Acceleration Curve).

  Rendering notes:
    - This template is consumed by render_deck.py, which substitutes the
      twenty-one tokens above from metrics.json and writes the result
      into acceleration/executive-presentation.html.
    - Each MULT token expands to either a numeric multiplier (e.g.,
      "3.2") OR the literal phrase "Insufficient signal — <reason>".
      The trailing "×" (U+00D7, multiplication sign — NOT the ASCII
      letter "x") in the template is rendered as-is for metrics 1, 2,
      3, 4, 5, 7. The renderer is responsible for stripping or hiding
      the suffix when the value is non-numeric (e.g., by substituting
      an empty string for MULT and rendering only the canonical phrase
      elsewhere). The "Insufficient signal" phrasing is canonical per
      AAP §0.7.2.1 and MUST NOT be replaced by editorial framing such
      as "unavailable" or "missing".
    - Metric 6 (Flow Distribution) is a work-type mix and is reported
      as a point-difference string (e.g., "Δ feat +12pp, fix −8pp" or
      "see Deep-Dive 6"), not a single scalar multiplier. The row for
      Metric 6 therefore has NO trailing × after {{M6_MULT}} — note the
      asymmetry below and AAP Phase 6 of the slide-9 spec.
    - Each CONF token expands to the CSS class suffix
      ("high" | "medium" | "low"), so the rendered span becomes
      <span class="confidence-low">Low</span>. The confidence badge
      styles are defined in acceleration/templates/deck/theme.css
      (.confidence-high / .confidence-medium / .confidence-low).
    - Per the AAP Confidence Rubric (§0.8.3): a metric derived from
      direct issue-tracker counts is High; a metric approximated from
      git commit patterns is Medium; a metric inferred from indirect
      proxies is Low. Confidence is assigned by the extractor at
      runtime based on the actual data source used — the template only
      surfaces the resolved class and label.
    - The renderer is the single source of truth (metrics.json); the
      multipliers shown here MUST be identical to the values reported
      in acceleration-report.md (Rule 4 — Internal Consistency,
      verified by verify_report.py which parses both the rendered
      Markdown and this rendered HTML and asserts equality).
    - Tone discipline (Rule 2 — Factual-Neutral): the metric labels
      are the canonical Flow Framework names — no editorial qualifiers
      such as "impressive", "significant", or "remarkable" appear on
      this slide.
    - Body word count outside the <table>: "Flow Framework" +
      "Flow Metrics (1–7)" = 5 words, well under the Rule 5 cap of 40.
-->
<section class="content-slide">
  <span class="eyebrow">Flow Framework</span>
  <h3>Flow Metrics (1–7)</h3>
  <table class="metric-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>#</th><th>Metric</th><th>Multiplier</th><th>Confidence</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1</td><td>Flow Load</td><td>{{M1_MULT}}×</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M1_CONF}}">{{M1_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>2</td><td>Flow Velocity</td><td>{{M2_MULT}}×</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M2_CONF}}">{{M2_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>3</td><td>Flow Predictability</td><td>{{M3_MULT}}×</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M3_CONF}}">{{M3_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>4</td><td>Flow Active</td><td>{{M4_MULT}}×</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M4_CONF}}">{{M4_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>5</td><td>Flow Efficiency</td><td>{{M5_MULT}}×</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M5_CONF}}">{{M5_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>6</td><td>Flow Distribution</td><td>{{M6_MULT}}</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M6_CONF}}">{{M6_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>7</td><td>Flow Time</td><td>{{M7_MULT}}×</td><td><span class="confidence-{{M7_CONF}}">{{M7_CONF_LABEL}}</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>
